    },
    "message": "Keep a world's entities in Rust rows, with the dataclasses as their mirror\n\nRust now holds AgentState, NeedState, FacilityState, StaffState,\nSupportRequestState and ActiveTask of a world in typed rows\n(native/src/state/entities.rs, from WorldCore). The maps are IdMap(dict): reads\nare inherited, writes attach and detach. An attached object's __setattr__, its\nTrackedList ID lists and WorldState.__setattr__ forward every write. No rule\nreads the rows yet, and no result changes.\n\nThe objects stay dataclasses instead of PyO3 windows: a window read cost 21-44 ns\nagainst 8-11 ns, Python keeps the exact value a row can't hold, and there is one\nclass to keep right. A value that does not fit taints the store, kernels get\nUnsupported and Python rules run on the objects with their own errors.\n\nasdict on staff, tasks, zones, edges and needs becomes to_dict().\nWith SHELTERSIM_NATIVE=0 these stay plain dicts and dataclasses.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
